@startuml
title Monitor Mode - Synchronisation Trigger Sources

rectangle "Monitor loop" as Loop
rectangle "Synchronisation engine" as Sync
rectangle "Local filesystem\ninotify" as Inotify
rectangle "Microsoft Graph\nWebSocket / Socket.IO" as WS
rectangle "Microsoft Graph\nWebhook subscription" as WH
rectangle "monitor_interval\nscheduled cycle" as Timer
rectangle "System-time / service\nsafety gate" as Gate

Inotify --> Loop : local change signal
WS --> Loop : remote change signal
WH --> Loop : remote change signal
Timer --> Loop : scheduled sync due
Loop --> Gate : validate before remote action
Gate --> Sync : safe to continue
Gate ..> Loop : defer and retry later

note right of Inotify
  Local filesystem monitoring is not initialised
  when ~--download-only is active.
end note

note right of WS
  Used only when ~--upload-only is not active,
  the linked libcurl build supports WebSockets,
  WebSocket support is not disabled, and
  webhook mode is not configured.
end note

note right of WH
  Optional alternative remote notification path.
  Not used with ~--upload-only. Webhook and
  WebSocket modes are not active together.
end note

note bottom of Loop
  Signals cause earlier reconciliation; monitor_interval remains
  the scheduled idle-sync cadence rather than a minimum delay.
end note
@enduml
